---
// Professional section — only shown in pro mode (.wp-page.is-pro), revealed
// when the visitor picks the practitioner door. Content distilled from the
// practitioner material in WNPractice: how the somatic disciplines you already
// know map onto voice work. Plain (CSS-revealed) rather than GSAP-scroll-
// revealed, so toggling it on never leaves anything stuck hidden.
const cards = [
  {
    icon: 'ph-heartbeat',
    title: 'Connected and soft — not catharsis',
    body: 'You stay ventral — shoulders soft, jaw soft — and put the charge into the tone, rather than discharging it. You’re not embodying the activation; you’re giving it a sound.',
  },
  {
    icon: 'ph-arrows-clockwise',
    title: 'Oscillation & pendulation',
    body: 'The same disciplines you already work with: the wide arc of activation then regulation, and the in-the-moment move toward the difficult and deliberately back to safety. Always inside the window of tolerance.',
  },
  {
    icon: 'ph-drop-half',
    title: 'The voice as built-in titration',
    body: 'The voice is a wise gatekeeper. It regulates both what surfaces and how intensely — the dose stays “just right.” You’re working with a system that already self-doses, not prying a lid off.',
  },
  {
    icon: 'ph-hand-eye',
    title: 'Attunement over protocol',
    body: 'The Cup: empty, cupped hands receiving the next move. You hold plans lightly and let it fill one step at a time. Information is received, not grabbed.',
  },
];
---

<section class="wp-practice wp-pro" id="for-practitioners" aria-label="For practitioners">
  <div class="wp-practice-inner">
    <div class="wp-practice-head">
      <div class="wp-eyebrow">If you come from somatic work</div>
      <h2>You already carry the map.<br /><em>Here’s where the voice fits.</em></h2>
      <p class="wp-practice-lead">
        Sound sits between the body and talk — much of the body’s access without
        the exposure of hands-on work, much of the articulacy of talk without
        routing everything through narrative. In the workshop you feel the
        method from the inside; here’s the shape of what you’d be holding.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="wp-practice-grid">
      {cards.map((c) => (
        <article class="wp-practice-card">
          <i class={`ph-light ${c.icon}`}></i>
          <h3>{c.title}</h3>
          <p>{c.body}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>

    <p class="wp-practice-foot">
      You can’t hold this for someone else until you’ve let it work on you first
      — which is exactly what the live hour is for.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
